    "summary": "Made from &#039;ie&#039;ie plant (freycinetia arborea), the olona plant, pearlshell, seeds, dog teeth and feathers from the i&#039;iwi and o&#039;o bird. A basketry frame made from intertwined, split aerial roots of ie&#039;ie plant is covered with a fibre netting made from the olona plant. Thousands of tiny feathers from the i&#039;iwi and o&#039;o birds are attached to this netting. Pearlshell, seeds and dog teeth and also attached and pearlshell eyes are held in place by wooden pegs, which also act as pupils.",
